# Call-site ledger of json-repair at f13a96b9c7ef0f590bc647e7c5424560b948462e.
# Drafted with a scratch script for the plain entries, then read entry by entry against the source; judgements in json-repair.md.
#
# The analysed package is src/json_repair under the root "." (module names
# src.json_repair.*). Supported versions: Python 3.10 and later
# (pyproject.toml, requires-python = ">=3.10").
#
# Where StringFileWrapper is: a StringFileWrapper is made only by
# JSONParser.__init__ (json_parser.py:62) and stored in JSONParser.json_str; a
# client can also pass one as json_str (JSONParser and StringFileWrapper are
# public, and the annotation is `str | StringFileWrapper`). json_str is
# reassigned only to str values (parse_object.py:239, 342). So the
# StringFileWrapper candidates are callees only where the operand is a
# parser's json_str (self.json_str, parser.json_str, the local alias json_str
# of _try_parse_simple_quoted_string) outside an isinstance(..., str) guard,
# or the wrapper itself (self[i], len(self) in StringFileWrapper); those sites
# accept them explicitly.
default reject src.json_repair.utils.string_file_wrapper.StringFileWrapper.__getitem__: the subscripted object is not a StringFileWrapper: it is a typing construct in an annotation, or a str, list, dict, tuple or schema value; the sites whose operand is a parser's json_str (outside an isinstance str guard) or the wrapper itself accept the candidate explicitly
default reject src.json_repair.utils.string_file_wrapper.StringFileWrapper.__len__: the operand of this truth test, len() or other builtin is not a StringFileWrapper (a str, list, dict, set, tuple, int, bool, None, schema value or client object); no truth test in the package tests json_str, and the len() sites whose argument is a parser's json_str or the wrapper itself accept the candidate explicitly
default reject src.json_repair.utils.string_file_wrapper.StringFileWrapper.__setitem__: the package never assigns an item of a StringFileWrapper: json_str is only reassigned as a whole (parse_object.py:239, 342); the item assignments here store into dicts and lists
default reject src.json_repair.utils.constants.MissingValueType.__repr__: no value that is formatted, printed, converted with str() or %-formatted here is MISSING_VALUE: the package passes MISSING_VALUE only to SchemaRepairer.repair_value (parse_object.py:312), and its tests pass it inside a dict to the same method (tests/test_schema_repairer.py:479-480); on every path repair_value replaces it (normalize_missing_values, _fill_missing or a nested repair_value) before anything formats it; the operands are strs, ints, schema values and exceptions, and every `%` is an integer remainder

